text:
maria: Heads-up — I'm landing a docs PR today to deprecate legacy variants for aurora-x and aurora-lite. Need callouts, migration snippets, and a short compatibility note. @kevin @ashley can you eyeball the SDK snippets? PR: https://github.com/redwood/inference-docs/pull/4287
kevin: On it. I'll check the migration snippet for SDK v3 -> v4. Anything we need to call out for runtime fallback behavior?
maria: Yes — mention the quantized fallback mapping: `aurora-x-quant` -> `aurora-x-compat-q4_0`. Also call out sequence ceiling behavior (old docs said 4096, new runtime supports up to 8192 depending on variant). Add a short sentence about results varying by batch size.
ashley: I can add an embeddings + fallback example. Prefer to show the `client.models.getVariant()` helper and then a `generate` call. Keeps it concrete for engineers.
samir: Quick ask — can we hold off deprecating aurora-lite3b in the public model card until runtime confirms there are no pinned instances? Last update mentioned some customers with pinned variants.
maria: Good catch. I'll ping runtime and prod-ops before the deprecation banner goes live. For now the PR can include the deprecation note but hidden behind a banner that we'll flip later.
docs-bot: Deploy preview: https://deploy-preview.redwood-docs.io/pr-4287 is live :eyes:
jen: Small nit in the model card JSON example — replace `sequence_length_limit` with `max_sequence_length` key (we standardized that last quarter).
kevin: Also need to sync the model catalog table (CSV) with the new limits. I'll open a follow-up PR to update the CSV and the generated table scripts.
ashley: Pasting SDK snippet I added for quick review:
```js
// SDK v4 example: resolve variant with fallback
const varName = await client.models.resolveVariant('aurora-x', { preferQuantized: true });
try {
  const out = await client.generate({ model: varName, input: prompt });
  console.log(out.text);
} catch (e) {
  // fallback to compat variant
  const fallback = 'aurora-x-compat-q4_0';
  const out2 = await client.generate({ model: fallback, input: prompt });
  console.log(out2.text);
}
```
maria: That looks good. Can you also add a one-line note showing the CLI variant alias for folks using curl? e.g., `--model aurora-x:compat-q4_0`
samir: Prod-ops replied — safe to proceed with docs but hold the deprecation banner flip until Friday to give teams time to patch pinned configs.
maria: Great. I'll update the PR to leave the banner flagged and add a TODO with the Friday date. :thumbsup:
kevin: One more nit — update the benchmark section to include a small table row: quantized throughput vs fp16 at batch sizes 1/8/32. Mention "results vary by hardware".
docs-bot: Preview build passed and link updated (CI #11245).
maria: Thanks all — I'll make the small edits, ping runtime for final thumbs up, and then we can merge the doc PR after the banner schedule is confirmed.
kevin: LGTM apart from the CSV sync.
ashley: Updated the snippet and added the CLI alias example.
samir: I'll follow up if prod-ops flags anything else.
maria: Closing loop tomorrow morning — thanks!
